WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:38.330
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:38.600 --> 01:40.880
The future content creator.

3
01:41.280 --> 01:42.000
This time,

4
01:42.080 --> 01:43.440
I'm not backing down.

5
01:43.880 --> 01:44.800
We have a problem!

6
01:44.800 --> 01:46.800
We need a new assistant by today.

7
01:47.240 --> 01:48.160
Ms. Alice,

8
01:48.160 --> 01:49.680
do you still want to work here?

9
01:49.920 --> 01:50.960
I've found someone.

10
01:51.440 --> 01:53.160
I hope she's not useless.

11
01:53.160 --> 01:54.120
Do you know who I am?

12
01:54.479 --> 01:55.280
Yes, I do.

13
01:55.360 --> 01:56.440
And from somewhere else?

14
01:58.039 --> 01:59.680
Isn't that Nannalin?

15
02:00.040 --> 02:01.240
Her zipper's open.

16
02:01.480 --> 02:02.600
Should I tell her?

17
02:03.320 --> 02:04.000
Next time,

18
02:04.000 --> 02:05.480
if you want to help me,

19
02:05.480 --> 02:06.400
ask me first.

20
02:07.040 --> 02:07.840
Understood.

21
02:18.360 --> 02:19.000
Alice.

22
02:19.000 --> 02:21.400
The perfume brand urgently needs slide five revised.

23
02:21.640 --> 02:22.920
Has the boss checked it yet?

24
02:22.920 --> 02:24.280
I'm counting on you.

25
02:26.600 --> 02:27.400
Alice!

26
02:28.840 --> 02:30.440
That influencer with 200,000 subscribers

27
02:30.520 --> 02:32.079
is asking for another two hours.

28
02:32.360 --> 02:34.760
Can you get Ms. Nannalin's approval?

29
02:35.160 --> 02:35.960
Please? Pretty please?

30
02:35.960 --> 02:36.760
I'm counting on you.

31
02:36.920 --> 02:37.720
Thank you!

32
02:40.160 --> 02:43.400
Yesterday's conversion summary is on this desk.

33
02:43.800 --> 02:45.840
Please have the boss sign it.

34
02:45.840 --> 02:47.680
Hey, wait...

35
02:47.680 --> 02:50.200
Slide five! Five!

36
02:54.079 --> 02:56.040
These are all the previous campaign records

37
02:56.040 --> 02:57.480
you need to read

38
02:57.480 --> 02:58.560
and understand.

39
03:01.080 --> 03:02.240
All of these?

40
03:03.440 --> 03:03.920
Yes.

41
03:03.920 --> 03:05.160
Every single one.

42
03:08.040 --> 03:09.280
200,000-subscriber influencer...

43
03:09.480 --> 03:11.240
Slide five! Slide five!

44
03:24.400 --> 03:27.079
Read everything and summarize the previous campaign issues.

45
03:27.079 --> 03:28.720
Separate the client contact list

46
03:28.720 --> 03:30.200
from the KOL list,

47
03:30.200 --> 03:32.280
and prioritize the most urgent tasks.

48
03:32.280 --> 03:33.800
I want it on my desk

49
03:33.800 --> 03:34.800
before noon.

50
03:40.720 --> 03:41.560
Understood.

51
04:06.800 --> 04:08.480
Save that shocked expression

52
04:08.840 --> 04:10.760
for when you actually mess up.

53
04:12.800 --> 04:13.680
Right now,

54
04:13.960 --> 04:16.279
you'd better start reading faster.

55
04:16.600 --> 04:18.880
I don't like working with slow people.

56
04:23.960 --> 04:24.880
Understood.

57
04:55.880 --> 04:56.960
If it were me,

58
04:57.159 --> 04:58.840
I'd sort these documents

59
04:59.240 --> 05:00.920
by how much damage each campaign caused,

60
05:02.280 --> 05:04.160
not by these cute

61
05:04.360 --> 05:05.600
pastel colors.

62
05:06.840 --> 05:08.920
Put any project that could cost the company

63
05:08.920 --> 05:10.680
hundreds of millions in penalties

64
05:10.680 --> 05:11.920
right on top.

65
05:12.520 --> 05:14.520
And the projects with fewer client complaints

66
05:14.640 --> 05:15.680
go at the bottom.

67
05:17.440 --> 05:19.080
Learn to rank your crises,

68
05:19.320 --> 05:21.880
and you'll know which file to take

69
05:21.880 --> 05:23.160
to Ms. Nannalin first.

70
05:28.600 --> 05:29.320
That's true.

71
05:29.320 --> 05:31.240
Sort them by severity.

72
05:33.560 --> 05:34.560
P'Nida!

73
05:34.560 --> 05:35.280
Thank you!

74
05:44.520 --> 05:45.880
Come to think of it,

75
05:46.280 --> 05:49.159
everyone here has such clearly defined roles.

76
05:49.320 --> 05:50.880
And they're all incredibly good at their jobs.

77
05:51.560 --> 05:53.040
Take P'Nida, for example.

78
05:53.040 --> 05:55.360
She may seem cold and stuck-up,

79
05:55.680 --> 05:58.440
but her advice about organizing files

80
05:58.720 --> 06:00.800
really saved my life.

81
06:00.800 --> 06:02.120
And P'Pim...

82
06:02.400 --> 06:03.920
She's so sweet!

83
06:03.920 --> 06:06.080
She's practically the AE team's guardian angel.

84
06:06.680 --> 06:09.880
She's always ready to rescue me from my mountain of work.

85
06:12.360 --> 06:13.120
And then...

86
06:13.120 --> 06:14.240
What about P'Nui?

87
06:14.360 --> 06:16.040
The one who's always snacking?

88
06:17.080 --> 06:19.520
Oh, she's a real character.

89
06:20.880 --> 06:24.840
She's the department's fake-news station and champion work-shirker.

90
06:47.440 --> 06:48.240
Excuse me.

91
06:54.200 --> 06:55.560
Where are the desks for the...

92
06:55.560 --> 06:59.080
exclusive content creator team?

93
06:59.080 --> 07:01.320
It's my first day here. I'm Mueanfan.

94
07:03.320 --> 07:04.120
Thank you!

95
07:22.840 --> 07:23.640
Pim!

96
07:24.320 --> 07:25.640
This year's new hires

97
07:26.120 --> 07:27.360
couldn't be more different.

98
07:27.760 --> 07:28.720
They're both making quite an entrance.

99
07:29.640 --> 07:30.440
How so?

100
07:31.400 --> 07:33.840
One showed up with her portfolio, ready to fight for her life.

101
07:34.440 --> 07:36.440
She looks like a soap-opera heroine,

102
07:36.440 --> 07:37.760
all set to be bossed around.

103
07:38.640 --> 07:39.760
And the other one

104
07:40.120 --> 07:41.920
is a pampered little princess.

105
07:43.320 --> 07:44.840
She looks like an intern with connections.

106
07:45.520 --> 07:46.840
Keep your voice down.

107
07:47.360 --> 07:50.159
It's barely morning and you're already gossiping?

108
07:50.640 --> 07:52.280
If anyone hears you,

109
07:52.520 --> 07:53.560
we'll all be in trouble.

110
07:53.880 --> 07:55.120
I don't care!

111
08:14.320 --> 08:15.760
How's it going, Alice?

112
08:16.840 --> 08:17.880
Oh, God...

113
08:18.040 --> 08:19.080
I'm almost there.

114
08:19.440 --> 08:21.880
Almost ready to melt into fertilizer right here.

115
08:22.360 --> 08:24.600
There's so much work, P'Pim!

116
08:25.200 --> 08:26.440
And it's all due by noon.

117
08:27.640 --> 08:30.280
Oh, come here. I'll help you.

118
08:30.440 --> 08:33.720
I'll list the campaigns and client names for you,

119
08:33.960 --> 08:36.320
so you won't waste time digging through those thick files.

120
08:37.440 --> 08:39.559
And I'll also...

121
08:39.799 --> 08:42.120
check each project's schedule for you.

122
08:42.200 --> 08:45.000
I'll see which ones need rates within half an hour,

123
08:45.440 --> 08:47.040
And which tasks would be disastrous if delayed.

124
08:47.200 --> 08:48.920
My soul will leave my body!

125
08:49.160 --> 08:50.560
That way, we'll finish everything before noon.

126
08:58.800 --> 08:59.600
Nui!

127
09:00.920 --> 09:03.000
You snuck off to the convenience store again, didn't you?

128
09:03.840 --> 09:06.200
Have you finished the design for page four?

129
09:06.960 --> 09:07.920
Oh, my goodness!

130
09:08.160 --> 09:10.520
What a terrible accusation, Pim!

131
09:10.720 --> 09:12.160
I wasn't slacking off.

132
09:12.400 --> 09:14.440
I was gathering supplies

133
09:14.600 --> 09:17.080
to recharge poor Alice!

134
09:17.080 --> 09:17.920
Look at her.

135
09:17.920 --> 09:21.000
She's working herself half to death.

136
09:25.240 --> 09:27.680
Oh! Thank you, P'Nui.

137
09:30.680 --> 09:31.800
But you know what?

138
09:31.800 --> 09:33.400
Let me tell you something.

139
09:33.400 --> 09:35.800
I think you've got some kind of magnetic energy,

140
09:35.800 --> 09:37.920
or maybe you're destined for something.

141
09:38.520 --> 09:40.760
On your very first day,

142
09:40.760 --> 09:43.080
you somehow attracted Ms. Nannalin's attention.

143
09:43.480 --> 09:44.320
She summoned you to her office,

144
09:45.320 --> 09:47.160
and gave you the toughest assignments

145
09:47.520 --> 09:49.160
first thing in the morning!

146
09:49.760 --> 09:50.560
Sigh...

147
09:50.680 --> 09:51.800
That's enough, Nui.

148
09:52.120 --> 09:53.720
What magnetic energy?

149
09:54.400 --> 09:56.040
The energy she's dealing with right now

150
09:56.600 --> 09:57.400
is called

151
09:57.400 --> 09:58.160
work

152
09:58.160 --> 09:58.960
over

153
09:58.960 --> 09:59.840
load!

154
10:00.520 --> 10:03.040
Why else would she be working herself into a frenzy?

155
10:04.200 --> 10:05.280
You've got a point.

156
10:06.080 --> 10:07.120
She's really in trouble.

157
10:08.360 --> 10:09.080
Seriously.

158
10:09.200 --> 10:10.840
There's definitely energy here.

159
10:10.840 --> 10:14.400
A whole avalanche of work on my desk!

160
10:15.120 --> 10:17.520
And I've only got one hour left.

161
10:17.520 --> 10:19.040
I don't know if I'll finish in time.

162
10:20.040 --> 10:21.080
Of course you will.

163
10:21.200 --> 10:22.600
You're in good hands.

164
10:22.600 --> 10:24.800
We'll both help you sort out the schedule.

165
10:25.960 --> 10:27.080
Let's finish our own work first.

166
10:27.680 --> 10:30.040
Before we help Alice, let's help ourselves first.

167
10:30.040 --> 10:31.960
The beauty campaign isn't finished yet.

168
10:31.960 --> 10:33.240
We'd better hurry.

169
10:33.240 --> 10:35.600
Otherwise, when Ms. Narin arrives,

170
10:35.600 --> 10:38.320
she'll come straight for us.

171
10:38.480 --> 10:40.120
We'll be dead!

172
10:43.120 --> 10:44.360
Oh, that's right!

173
10:44.360 --> 10:46.080
I completely forgot!

174
10:46.520 --> 10:47.880
Well, then...

175
10:48.400 --> 10:49.600
We'd better

176
10:49.760 --> 10:52.000
finish our own work first.

177
10:53.320 --> 10:54.720
Hang in there, Alice!

178
11:16.720 --> 11:17.520
Alice!

179
11:19.040 --> 11:20.920
I really need your help.

180
11:22.120 --> 11:23.680
Um, what's wrong?

181
11:24.800 --> 11:25.400
Well...

182
11:25.640 --> 11:28.280
I made a draft content file

183
11:28.280 --> 11:30.120
to send to the graphics team,

184
11:30.120 --> 11:32.120
but somehow it's disappeared.

185
11:32.120 --> 11:33.520
I checked the cloud,

186
11:33.960 --> 11:35.320
and I can't find it anywhere.

187
11:36.120 --> 11:39.720
Can you help me recover or find it?

188
11:46.320 --> 11:47.160
It's just that...

189
11:47.480 --> 11:49.880
I've still got a ton of work

190
11:49.880 --> 11:51.280
for Ms. Nannalin,

191
11:51.280 --> 11:52.920
and it's all due before noon.

192
11:53.760 --> 11:55.520
Please!

193
11:55.520 --> 11:57.560
Alice, please help me.

194
11:57.560 --> 12:00.000
It's my first day, and...

195
12:00.280 --> 12:01.640
I'm terrible with computers.

196
12:03.120 --> 12:04.600
I don't know who else to ask.

197
12:05.640 --> 12:08.680
If I can't submit the draft on time,

198
12:08.920 --> 12:10.480
I'm definitely going to get scolded.

199
12:11.280 --> 12:12.200
Please help me.

200
12:15.200 --> 12:16.920
Okay, okay. I'll

201
12:16.920 --> 12:19.560
check the trash folder for you.

202
12:33.080 --> 12:33.880
Okay.

203
12:33.880 --> 12:34.760
Thanks, Alice!

204
13:14.320 --> 13:15.680
Oh, Alice!

205
13:17.560 --> 13:19.480
I wasn't slacking off, sweetheart.

206
13:20.040 --> 13:21.160
I was just...

207
13:21.600 --> 13:22.400
low on sugar.

208
13:22.480 --> 13:23.160
My blood sugar dropped.

209
13:23.160 --> 13:25.080
You know, a sudden sugar crash?

210
13:25.440 --> 13:26.880
And it's break time anyway.

211
13:27.080 --> 13:27.880
I'm just taking a break

212
13:28.120 --> 13:30.440
to clear my mind and recharge my creativity.

213
13:30.600 --> 13:33.720
We're creating world-class art here!

214
13:34.440 --> 13:35.240
Believe me!

215
13:35.400 --> 13:39.440
I haven't even said a word yet!

216
13:41.960 --> 13:42.920
Nui!

217
13:44.400 --> 13:46.120
Sneaking off to slack again, I see.

218
13:46.560 --> 13:48.600
You're always the first to disappear.

219
13:50.320 --> 13:51.480
Seriously, tell me something.

220
13:52.000 --> 13:54.400
Do you have some kind of slacker radar

221
13:54.520 --> 13:55.920
implanted in your eyeballs?

222
13:56.240 --> 13:57.360
You're always catching me!

223
13:58.280 --> 13:59.400
Am I really that obvious?

224
14:01.680 --> 14:03.440
You've been obvious from the start.

225
14:04.240 --> 14:05.440
Your face

226
14:05.440 --> 14:08.320
has 'slacker' written all over it.

227
14:08.760 --> 14:09.960
Anyone who can't see that

228
14:09.960 --> 14:11.120
must be blind.

229
14:12.040 --> 14:13.360
Where? Can I wipe it off?

230
14:14.600 --> 14:17.200
Finish eating and go fix that draft. Now!

231
14:18.080 --> 14:19.200
But I'm hungry!

232
14:26.400 --> 14:27.960
Hello, Ms. Nannalin.

233
14:29.000 --> 14:30.040
You're out of iced tea?

234
14:31.480 --> 14:33.320
Of course. I'll bring it right away.

235
14:42.480 --> 14:44.120
See you, P'Pim, P'Nui!

236
14:45.960 --> 14:46.760
Go on!

237
14:50.960 --> 14:51.760
Is it good?

238
14:51.840 --> 14:53.160
Delicious. Want some?

239
14:54.560 --> 14:55.680
So rich!

240
15:00.480 --> 15:02.800
But the person who stresses me out the most

241
15:03.280 --> 15:05.080
is Ms. Nannalin.

242
15:09.920 --> 15:10.720
Here you go.

243
15:44.000 --> 15:45.080
The structure is acceptable.

244
15:47.200 --> 15:50.000
You've identified the campaign's main problems well,

245
15:54.120 --> 15:55.320
but it's not sharp enough.

246
15:57.080 --> 15:57.800
You have plenty of data,

247
15:58.720 --> 16:00.920
but lack strategic analysis.

248
16:02.960 --> 16:04.120
You can identify problems,

249
16:04.720 --> 16:06.720
but not practical solutions.

250
16:13.920 --> 16:15.160
Take it back and revise it.

251
16:16.320 --> 16:18.840
Divide your recommendations into three phases:

252
16:19.760 --> 16:20.920
most urgent,

253
16:20.920 --> 16:22.560
medium priority,

254
16:22.560 --> 16:24.800
and contingency plan.

255
16:27.120 --> 16:28.880
I'll revise it as quickly as possible.

256
16:36.800 --> 16:39.520
If you want to secure your place here,

257
16:41.160 --> 16:43.760
you need to understand that in the real working world,

258
16:43.800 --> 16:47.280
effort alone is never enough.

259
16:47.720 --> 16:50.280
Because everyone is trying hard.

260
16:53.840 --> 16:56.640
I don't need to see your sweat.

261
16:57.760 --> 16:59.720
I need quality results.

262
17:05.040 --> 17:05.720
Understood.

263
17:05.720 --> 17:08.480
I'll submit a much sharper draft

264
17:08.480 --> 17:11.520
before noon, Ms. Nannalin.

265
17:21.440 --> 17:24.359
Wow, this doesn't sound like a first day at work.

266
17:24.800 --> 17:26.839
You're like a little lamb

267
17:27.599 --> 17:29.760
thrown into a tiger's cage.

268
17:30.160 --> 17:31.440
But what's amazing

269
17:31.440 --> 17:35.920
is that the tiger's cage smells of hot tea!

270
17:39.920 --> 17:44.520
She's so intimidating I almost forgot how to breathe.

271
17:45.280 --> 17:47.040
She's the kind of boss who's...

272
17:48.840 --> 17:49.920
Too beautiful.

273
17:50.760 --> 17:51.320
I mean,

274
17:52.000 --> 17:54.400
her beauty doesn't match how ruthless she is.

275
17:54.600 --> 17:56.880
She's as strict as a drill sergeant.

276
17:58.120 --> 17:59.200
Beautiful?

277
18:00.360 --> 18:01.320
How beautiful?

278
18:02.000 --> 18:03.960
I thought she was an evil witch.

279
18:04.640 --> 18:05.480
How come

280
18:05.480 --> 18:08.120
she's suddenly too beautiful as well,

281
18:08.120 --> 18:08.720
Ms. Assistant?

282
18:08.920 --> 18:09.720
Hmph!

283
18:10.440 --> 18:12.160
I'm talking about her suits!

284
18:12.160 --> 18:15.080
Her suits are perfectly tailored every day.

285
18:16.120 --> 18:16.920
Beautiful.

286
18:19.480 --> 18:20.360
Way too beautiful.

287
18:26.920 --> 18:27.680
Ugh.

288
18:28.560 --> 18:29.480
This sucks.

289
18:30.080 --> 18:31.840
If I didn't have another event to attend,

290
18:32.080 --> 18:34.160
I'd keep you here all night

291
18:34.160 --> 18:35.480
so you could blow off some steam.

292
18:36.160 --> 18:37.880
Go take care of work first.

293
18:37.880 --> 18:39.480
We can meet anytime.

294
18:40.720 --> 18:41.840
And you, too.

295
18:42.600 --> 18:45.080
Don't work yourself to death without resting.

296
18:45.560 --> 18:48.520
You look like a zombie after just one day.

297
18:49.280 --> 18:52.200
After a month, your soul might leave your body!

298
18:53.520 --> 18:55.640
I'll get used to it.

299
18:56.520 --> 18:59.240
It's only my first day of getting beaten down.

300
18:59.240 --> 19:03.440
My body will build up immunity eventually.

301
19:05.320 --> 19:07.080
Whatever helps you sleep at night.

302
19:08.040 --> 19:09.560
But let me warn you:

303
19:09.560 --> 19:12.000
Work hard all you want,

304
19:12.000 --> 19:13.880
but don't tie yourself

305
19:14.560 --> 19:16.200
or your heart

306
19:17.000 --> 19:20.360
to that beautiful boss.

307
19:21.040 --> 19:23.480
I'm warning you for your own good.

308
19:23.880 --> 19:24.840
Hey, hey!

309
19:40.000 --> 19:41.520
Hello, Ms. Nannalin.

310
19:42.000 --> 19:45.040
Please find Ms. Ratee's background and personal information.

311
19:45.440 --> 19:46.440
I want an in-depth profile,

312
19:46.640 --> 19:47.760
including her personal lifestyle,

313
19:47.760 --> 19:49.200
her favorite luxury brands,

314
19:49.200 --> 19:51.680
and most importantly,

315
19:51.680 --> 19:54.880
find some interesting talking points

316
19:54.880 --> 19:56.640
I can use to open a conversation

317
19:56.640 --> 19:58.240
and break the ice with her.

318
19:59.720 --> 20:00.600
Um, of course.

319
20:00.760 --> 20:02.640
How urgently do you need it,

320
20:02.880 --> 20:03.880
Ms. Nannalin?

321
20:04.160 --> 20:05.680
Before I have to ask for it.

322
20:05.680 --> 20:06.120
What?

323
20:10.240 --> 20:11.040
Why?

324
20:12.280 --> 20:13.360
You're in trouble now.

325
20:17.040 --> 20:20.880
An assignment that requires psychic powers?

326
20:23.520 --> 20:26.200
Someone else would've thrown their resignation in her face.

327
20:27.400 --> 20:27.880
Hey!

328
20:28.080 --> 20:29.680
It's really fate!

329
20:30.560 --> 20:32.080
Good luck, my friend!

330
20:32.520 --> 20:33.880
I'm rooting for you!

331
20:34.760 --> 20:37.080
I've got to find information for Ms. Narin first.

332
20:37.400 --> 20:38.560
Okay, see you!

333
20:38.680 --> 20:39.480
Yeah, yeah!

334
20:40.040 --> 20:41.000
Thank you, thank you!

335
20:42.080 --> 20:43.360
No sleep for you tonight.

336
20:47.440 --> 20:47.800
Hey!

337
20:48.440 --> 20:48.880
Wait!

338
20:49.560 --> 20:52.480
At least pay your bill first!

339
20:57.680 --> 20:58.880
Excuse me.

340
21:15.480 --> 21:17.480
Are you going to stand there all day?

341
21:20.040 --> 21:20.560
Um...

342
21:21.200 --> 21:22.000
I'm sorry.

343
21:27.840 --> 21:29.120
These are

344
21:29.520 --> 21:32.880
the documents I prepared on Ms. Ratee.

345
21:33.560 --> 21:34.560
They cover her background,

346
21:34.560 --> 21:36.480
lifestyle, favorite brands,

347
21:36.480 --> 21:38.040
and favorite places.

348
21:39.040 --> 21:43.080
I've also included some conversation starters.

349
21:50.160 --> 21:52.520
Ms. Ratee dislikes aggressive salespeople.

350
21:54.080 --> 21:54.880
Oh.

351
21:55.600 --> 21:56.320
Okay.

352
21:56.320 --> 21:59.080
She dislikes scripted compliments.

353
21:59.960 --> 22:00.760
Understood.

354
22:01.120 --> 22:03.920
And she dislikes people who think quiet luxury

355
22:03.920 --> 22:05.480
just means wearing beige.

356
22:06.120 --> 22:06.920
Understood.

357
22:07.320 --> 22:08.480
You're coming with me tomorrow.

358
22:09.440 --> 22:10.240
Pardon?

359
22:14.560 --> 22:15.320
Um...

360
22:15.320 --> 22:16.360
You mean...

361
22:16.640 --> 22:18.320
I'm going with you, Ms. Nannalin?

362
22:18.320 --> 22:19.120
Yes.

363
22:19.480 --> 22:21.640
To meet Ms. Ratee together?

364
22:24.280 --> 22:26.400
Did I say something else?

365
22:28.600 --> 22:29.400
No.

366
22:32.760 --> 22:34.080
You don't need to talk much.

367
22:34.760 --> 22:36.480
Tomorrow, your job is to

368
22:36.480 --> 22:36.720
watch,

369
22:36.880 --> 22:37.360
listen,

370
22:37.440 --> 22:38.800
and remember.

371
22:41.280 --> 22:43.120
Answer only if I ask you something.

372
22:44.280 --> 22:46.840
If I don't ask, don't speak.

373
22:47.160 --> 22:47.960
Okay.

374
22:52.320 --> 22:53.640
Dress nicely tomorrow.

375
22:55.160 --> 22:55.960
Huh?

376
22:56.640 --> 22:57.640
Elegantly but professionally.

377
22:58.320 --> 23:00.000
Not like you're going to a party.

378
23:01.560 --> 23:02.840
And don't be so conservative

379
23:03.480 --> 23:05.000
that you look like you're taking a civil service exam.

380
23:06.040 --> 23:06.480
Ah.

381
23:06.600 --> 23:07.840
Understood.

382
23:08.440 --> 23:10.160
Elegant and professional.

383
23:10.160 --> 23:11.040
Not a party outfit,

384
23:11.680 --> 23:13.880
and not too formal either.

385
23:30.560 --> 23:31.960
Your heart is beating so fast.

386
23:36.160 --> 23:36.760
Oh.

387
23:37.600 --> 23:41.080
I'm excited about tomorrow's meeting.

388
23:42.200 --> 23:43.240
Just like that night.

389
23:47.560 --> 23:48.880
Ms. Nannalin...

390
23:49.520 --> 23:50.560
You remember?

391
23:53.160 --> 23:54.640
Did you really think I'd forget

392
23:54.640 --> 23:56.760
someone who saved my dress from disaster

393
23:58.080 --> 23:59.080
and also

394
23:59.080 --> 24:00.840
ruined my plans

395
24:00.840 --> 24:02.320
so easily?

396
24:07.680 --> 24:09.080
Um, I thought...

397
24:22.200 --> 24:23.680
Ms. Nannalin...

398
24:24.200 --> 24:25.920
Dress nicely tomorrow.

399
24:26.160 --> 24:27.840
And pay attention to

400
24:28.080 --> 24:29.080
what I'm going to teach you.

401
24:32.720 --> 24:33.520
Yes.

402
24:35.120 --> 24:36.080
You may go home now.

403
24:38.800 --> 24:41.400
See you tomorrow at eight sharp.

404
24:44.040 --> 24:44.840
Yes.

405
24:58.400 --> 24:59.600
She actually remembers?

406
25:06.600 --> 25:07.560
It's a business meeting.

407
25:07.560 --> 25:08.880
Just a business meeting.

408
25:08.880 --> 25:10.160
Don't think about the kiss.

409
25:10.680 --> 25:11.920
Absolutely don't think about the kiss.

410
25:13.560 --> 25:14.360
Oh, God!

411
25:15.640 --> 25:16.720
I've already thought about it!

412
25:20.600 --> 25:22.400
Do you know the biggest twist in the series? Yeah?

413
25:22.400 --> 25:22.880
The male lead...

414
25:22.880 --> 25:25.080
Guess who he kisses in the cave instead of me?

415
25:25.440 --> 25:26.680
The second male lead! Oh, God!

416
25:26.840 --> 25:29.280
I was shocked! Why didn't he kiss me?

417
25:29.280 --> 25:30.760
What show were you even watching?

418
25:30.760 --> 25:32.600
I want to be in it so badly!

419
25:32.600 --> 25:34.080
People really get obsessed, huh?

420
25:34.400 --> 25:35.400
Oh, my goodness!

421
25:36.840 --> 25:39.600
Alice is dressed like a proper young manager today!

422
25:40.400 --> 25:41.760
What do you think? Does it work?

423
25:42.840 --> 25:43.880
Very polished!

424
25:44.280 --> 25:45.520
Do you have a date,

425
25:45.520 --> 25:47.360
or is it a special occasion?

426
25:47.640 --> 25:47.800
What?

427
25:47.800 --> 25:50.320
Alice, of all people,

428
25:50.320 --> 25:51.480
is dressed so neatly,

429
25:51.480 --> 25:53.960
from her collar down to her trousers.

430
25:53.960 --> 25:55.760
With an outfit like this,

431
25:56.680 --> 25:59.440
I'm a hundred percent sure she's meeting a client

432
25:59.960 --> 26:01.280
with Ms. Nannalin.

433
26:01.880 --> 26:02.960
You know too much!

434
26:05.600 --> 26:06.400
You there.

435
26:07.880 --> 26:08.680
Yes?

436
26:08.720 --> 26:10.960
If you're meeting a client with Ms. Nannalin today,

437
26:11.400 --> 26:12.440
make sure

438
26:12.640 --> 26:14.800
you're not wearing strong perfume,

439
26:15.240 --> 26:17.360
especially anything sickly sweet

440
26:17.760 --> 26:19.360
or a trendy, overpowering fragrance.

441
26:19.960 --> 26:22.280
Our client is a VIP

442
26:22.760 --> 26:24.600
and very sensitive to scents.

443
26:26.320 --> 26:27.480
Of course, of course.

444
26:27.480 --> 26:29.480
I'm not wearing any perfume today.

445
26:29.480 --> 26:30.480
Thank you for warning me.

446
26:40.240 --> 26:41.040
Alice.

447
26:42.680 --> 26:43.480
Um...

448
26:45.200 --> 26:47.240
I need another favor.

449
26:49.040 --> 26:51.080
I was trying to upload

450
26:51.080 --> 26:53.920
my idea summary to the shared drive, but...

451
26:54.800 --> 26:56.600
somehow

452
26:56.600 --> 27:00.280
it ended up in the account folder.

453
27:00.280 --> 27:01.240
I don't know how to move it.

454
27:01.240 --> 27:04.040
I tried, but I couldn't do it.

455
27:04.680 --> 27:06.680
Could you help me?

456
27:08.360 --> 27:09.160
Hmm.

457
27:11.400 --> 27:13.720
Okay. I'll move it for you.

458
27:22.840 --> 27:26.440
There. I've moved it to the creative content folder.

459
27:26.440 --> 27:28.600
That was so fast!

460
27:28.600 --> 27:29.840
Thanks, Alice!

461
27:29.840 --> 27:32.280
You're the kindest and sweetest person!

462
27:32.280 --> 27:32.880
Thank you!

463
27:47.880 --> 27:50.160
Here's the detailed profile summary

464
27:50.160 --> 27:53.720
and the suggested conversation starters for Ms. Ratee.

465
28:13.320 --> 28:14.440
Good summary.

466
28:17.480 --> 28:19.920
You've accurately identified her sophisticated tastes,

467
28:20.560 --> 28:22.640
her appreciation for intricate design,

468
28:23.360 --> 28:26.600
and the way she socializes.

469
28:27.720 --> 28:29.440
Especially your suggestions

470
28:29.920 --> 28:32.560
for icebreakers.

471
28:35.480 --> 28:36.680
Thank you.

472
28:37.280 --> 28:39.680
Actually, after reviewing her background

473
28:39.680 --> 28:41.440
and lifestyle,

474
28:41.440 --> 28:43.840
I think it's more than personal preferences.

475
28:44.240 --> 28:45.440
Ms. Ratee

476
28:45.440 --> 28:46.960
carefully decides

477
28:46.960 --> 28:49.640
how she wants people to see her,

478
28:49.720 --> 28:53.040
and who gets to see which side of her.

479
28:59.160 --> 29:00.760
You're starting to understand.

480
29:10.960 --> 29:12.800
Tea.

481
29:16.160 --> 29:17.080
Of course.

482
29:17.080 --> 29:19.480
I'll bring you hot tea at the perfect temperature

483
29:19.480 --> 29:20.680
and have it on your desk

484
29:20.680 --> 29:22.080
within three minutes.

485
29:30.480 --> 29:32.080
Water at just the right temperature,

486
29:32.080 --> 29:33.400
steeped perfectly, not too weak or bitter, sweet or cold.

487
29:33.400 --> 29:34.920
Not too weak or bitter,

488
29:34.920 --> 29:36.800
not sweet or cold.

489
29:47.440 --> 29:49.160
Are you brewing tea,

490
29:49.160 --> 29:51.240
or reciting some kind of spirit-summoning ritual?

491
29:52.080 --> 29:53.800
I'm making tea for Ms. Nannalin.

492
29:54.360 --> 29:55.760
Then it's not tea-making.

493
29:56.320 --> 29:57.600
It's preparing a sacred offering!

494
29:58.280 --> 30:00.320
Oh, P'Nui!

495
30:01.040 --> 30:01.600
Sigh...

496
30:01.720 --> 30:03.400
I'd better stop bothering you.

497
30:03.400 --> 30:06.120
Our rookie is about to enter the battlefield. Respect!

498
30:06.120 --> 30:08.720
I'm showing respect!

499
30:13.440 --> 30:15.040
Great color, great aroma.

500
30:20.200 --> 30:21.960
Oh!

501
30:28.960 --> 30:29.960
Congratulations!

502
30:29.960 --> 30:33.480
You've passed the first trial of the Witch of Lune!

503
30:35.160 --> 30:37.200
I haven't even given it to Ms. Nannalin yet.

504
30:37.440 --> 30:38.320
Then you haven't passed yet.

505
30:38.640 --> 30:40.960
You've only made it through the preliminaries.

506
30:50.360 --> 30:52.400
Ms. Ratee is here. What?

507
30:53.280 --> 30:54.480
We have to go meet her.

508
30:55.320 --> 30:56.320
Right now?

509
30:57.040 --> 30:58.680
We can wait until tomorrow,

510
30:58.680 --> 30:59.520
if you prefer.

511
31:05.080 --> 31:07.400
And your tea was going so well today.

512
31:11.280 --> 31:12.560
Please take care of this, P'Nui.

513
31:16.920 --> 31:17.720
Oh, dear.

514
31:18.640 --> 31:20.560
A prince born at the wrong time.

515
31:25.880 --> 31:26.680
Breathe.

516
31:27.720 --> 31:28.520
Yes?

517
31:29.760 --> 31:36.400
Today you watch, listen, and remember. Don't speak unless I ask.

518
31:38.040 --> 31:38.880
Understood.

519
31:49.240 --> 31:49.960
Hello.

520
31:50.720 --> 31:53.360
I'm sorry I arrived early.

521
31:53.560 --> 31:54.680
Not at all.

522
31:54.680 --> 31:57.560
It's lovely to see you. Please have a seat.

523
32:05.120 --> 32:08.200
You look wonderful today, Ms. Ratee.

524
32:08.760 --> 32:11.680
Especially that Hermès scarf.

525
32:12.680 --> 32:15.880
The delicate print and lightweight fabric

526
32:15.880 --> 32:18.960
remind me of an afternoon in Kashmir.

527
32:20.480 --> 32:22.520
You have a keen eye, Ms. Nan.

528
32:23.440 --> 32:28.000
I chose this scarf because it reminded me of Kashmir, too.

529
32:29.440 --> 32:32.400
I never overlook beautiful things

530
32:33.360 --> 32:35.400
that have stories hidden in them.

531
32:40.920 --> 32:44.000
I'm launching a new cosmetics line of my own.

532
32:44.000 --> 32:46.120
And I'd love for Lune Agency

533
32:46.120 --> 32:49.640
to manage it and develop a strategy for the brand.

534
32:49.920 --> 32:52.040
That includes new product launches,

535
32:52.560 --> 32:55.480
KOL coordination and events,

536
32:55.480 --> 32:58.240
and especially media PR.

537
32:59.560 --> 33:02.320
That sounds like a fascinating project, Ms. Ratee.

538
33:03.400 --> 33:06.120
And when it comes to brand ambassadors,

539
33:06.440 --> 33:08.440
do you have anyone in mind?

540
33:09.800 --> 33:13.320
I'm considering Namhom and Preem.

541
33:14.640 --> 33:17.320
One is a hugely popular actress,

542
33:17.320 --> 33:18.560
and the other

543
33:18.560 --> 33:20.400
is a top beauty blogger.

544
33:21.280 --> 33:23.920
They both have strong fan bases,

545
33:23.920 --> 33:26.080
which would be great for a new brand.

546
33:28.200 --> 33:31.000
Those are interesting choices.

547
33:31.480 --> 33:34.160
So your cosmetics brand

548
33:34.640 --> 33:36.880
isn't just selling youthful beauty.

549
33:38.000 --> 33:40.000
It's selling confidence

550
33:40.480 --> 33:44.320
and the power of women who choose to care for themselves with taste,

551
33:45.080 --> 33:47.400
without seeking anyone else's approval.

552
33:48.440 --> 33:50.040
Exactly.

553
33:50.040 --> 33:53.080
This brand is a matter of pride for me.

554
33:55.000 --> 33:57.320
If I can make it successful,

555
33:58.080 --> 33:59.360
I hope

556
33:59.360 --> 34:02.160
someone as important as Ms. Rinrada

557
34:02.160 --> 34:03.760
will see what I'm capable of.

558
34:08.360 --> 34:09.159
I'm counting on you.

559
34:11.800 --> 34:12.600
Absolutely.

560
34:16.199 --> 34:17.480
Ms. Nannalin.

561
34:19.199 --> 34:20.639
You're incredible.

562
34:22.239 --> 34:23.320
Did you only just realize that?

563
34:25.520 --> 34:28.000
I've always known you were good.

564
34:28.000 --> 34:31.080
But today I saw for myself

565
34:31.080 --> 34:33.800
just how well you can read people.

566
34:33.800 --> 34:35.400
The scarf,

567
34:35.400 --> 34:37.000
Ms. Ratee,

568
34:37.000 --> 34:43.800
and the way you didn't have to sell anything to make her feel understood.

569
34:50.679 --> 34:51.560
Sorry.

570
34:53.239 --> 34:57.040
What you witnessed today wasn't a trick for flattering clients.

571
34:58.000 --> 35:01.760
It was listening beyond the words they say.

572
35:05.120 --> 35:06.120
Ms. Ratee

573
35:06.600 --> 35:09.560
doesn't just need us to sell lipstick.

574
35:10.760 --> 35:12.600
She needs this brand

575
35:12.600 --> 35:15.360
to prove something about who she is.

576
35:17.240 --> 35:19.600
You mean to Ms. Rinrada?

577
35:23.920 --> 35:25.520
Sorry.

578
35:26.840 --> 35:27.560
I shouldn't have...

579
35:27.880 --> 35:30.840
No, this time you're right.

580
35:32.600 --> 35:34.600
But even when you're right,

581
35:34.600 --> 35:36.280
you need to know when to keep it to yourself.

582
35:37.480 --> 35:39.200
Not every truth

583
35:39.200 --> 35:41.600
needs to be spoken immediately.

584
35:43.760 --> 35:44.720
I understand.

585
36:08.440 --> 36:09.600
Your lipstick...

586
36:14.200 --> 36:15.200
It's a pretty shade.

587
36:19.360 --> 36:20.360
It suits you.

588
36:33.160 --> 36:35.200
Is that still part of the lesson?

589
36:59.080 --> 37:00.760
Well, well, Ms. Assistant!

590
37:02.080 --> 37:05.040
You look awfully pleased with yourself.

591
37:06.000 --> 37:11.480
Is it the heat outside, or is there another reason your cheeks are red?

592
37:11.720 --> 37:12.520
Ah!

593
37:13.560 --> 37:15.760
You scared me, P'Nui!

594
37:16.880 --> 37:21.400
I was only asking whether the client meeting went well.

595
37:22.680 --> 37:24.600
Oh... yes, it did.

596
37:25.200 --> 37:26.800
Ms. Natty was really nice.

597
37:27.480 --> 37:28.960
Your voice is all squeaky.

598
37:29.120 --> 37:30.480
And that answer was suspiciously short.

599
37:30.800 --> 37:31.960
You're hiding something!

600
37:34.640 --> 37:35.320
Oh, come on!

601
37:35.640 --> 37:37.840
I need to upload these files to my computer.

602
37:43.280 --> 37:44.080
Hmm.

603
37:44.320 --> 37:46.320
That settles it. Something's going on.

604
37:46.640 --> 37:47.040
Hmph.

605
37:47.040 --> 37:49.000
Aren't you overthinking things, Nui?

606
37:49.600 --> 37:52.720
Alice might just have stayed up all night working.

607
37:52.720 --> 37:54.280
That could explain why she looks dazed and flushed.

608
37:55.080 --> 37:55.960
How can you be so sure?

609
37:56.520 --> 37:57.400
Do you have evidence?

610
37:58.000 --> 37:59.360
There goes your rumor mill again.

611
37:59.680 --> 38:01.840
The evidence is written all over Alice's face.

612
38:02.280 --> 38:03.040
Usually,

613
38:03.040 --> 38:05.000
when Ms. Nannalin gives her a hard time,

614
38:05.000 --> 38:08.240
she turns pale as a ghost.

615
38:08.240 --> 38:09.120
But look at her now!

616
38:09.120 --> 38:12.920
Rosy cheeks and dreamy eyes!

617
38:13.200 --> 38:16.920
She's acting exactly like someone who's fallen in love!

618
38:18.040 --> 38:20.320
Pim, let me warn you.

619
38:20.320 --> 38:23.960
Don't listen too much to Nui's fake-news channel.

620
38:23.960 --> 38:25.360
It'll rot your brain.

621
38:26.040 --> 38:27.720
Are you prejudiced against me?

622
38:27.880 --> 38:32.080
I've actually studied advanced office psychology!

623
38:32.080 --> 38:34.600
I may not look like it, but I read books!

624
38:34.600 --> 38:36.160
Alice's behavior

625
38:36.160 --> 38:37.800
is exactly what you see when someone

626
38:37.800 --> 38:40.360
tries to act normal,

627
38:40.360 --> 38:42.840
but just ends up looking even less normal.

628
38:44.720 --> 38:47.200
And here's the overview of our campaign.

629
38:47.200 --> 38:52.000
Our mood and tone will focus on fun, energy, and vibrancy.

630
38:52.000 --> 38:54.800
We'll bring youthful spirit to the world,

631
38:54.800 --> 38:56.840
with an emphasis on freshness,

632
38:56.840 --> 38:58.760
a full hundred percent.

633
38:58.760 --> 39:00.160
Thank you.

634
39:04.360 --> 39:05.160
Ms. Nui,

635
39:08.240 --> 39:11.600
if a woman older than your main target demographic

636
39:12.080 --> 39:13.320
saw this campaign,

637
39:14.440 --> 39:15.760
do you think she'd be interested

638
39:16.680 --> 39:19.160
in buying this cosmetics brand?

639
39:20.480 --> 39:24.640
But our primary target audience is

640
39:24.640 --> 39:26.880
university students to early-career women, Ms. Narin.

641
39:28.120 --> 39:30.160
Ms. Ratee's idea of freshness

642
39:30.480 --> 39:32.200
doesn't necessarily mean being young

643
39:32.400 --> 39:34.000
or being a teenager.

644
39:34.720 --> 39:36.800
A fresh start and a sense of renewal

645
39:36.800 --> 39:43.640
can belong to women of any age. A good cosmetics brand shouldn't build walls

646
39:44.680 --> 39:46.520
or exclude any group of women

647
39:47.400 --> 39:50.320
just because they aren't the market's ideal age.

648
39:53.440 --> 39:59.160
Ms. Ratee wants luxury, confidence, and results that reflect her identity.

649
40:00.680 --> 40:03.360
Revise this project's mood and tone.

650
40:04.000 --> 40:05.880
Add an element of accessible luxury,

651
40:06.760 --> 40:10.040
and bring out a mature, sophisticated freshness.

652
40:11.280 --> 40:13.040
Absolutely, Ms. Nannalin.

653
40:13.040 --> 40:15.200
That's a brilliant idea.

654
40:15.200 --> 40:18.160
My team and I will rework everything

655
40:18.880 --> 40:20.640
and make the concept as sharp as possible.

656
40:21.240 --> 40:22.040
Thank you.

657
40:23.520 --> 40:25.600
Please move quickly.

658
40:26.000 --> 40:29.200
This project is urgent and very important to our company.

659
40:30.120 --> 40:30.600
Of course.

660
40:30.760 --> 40:33.520
We'll get it done as soon as possible.

661
40:40.400 --> 40:42.920
Is something urgent, Ms. Rinrada?

662
40:45.240 --> 40:48.800
I heard the new cosmetics campaign

663
40:49.400 --> 40:51.720
you just had a meeting about

664
40:52.280 --> 40:53.920
belongs to Ms. Ratee. Is that right?

665
40:55.440 --> 40:56.240
Yes.

666
41:00.720 --> 41:01.880
That's rather strange.

667
41:03.560 --> 41:06.200
Someone as meticulous and ambitious as Ratee...

668
41:07.800 --> 41:09.760
Why would she come to an agency like ours?

669
41:15.480 --> 41:21.760
Do you have insider information or concerns about this project, Ms. Rinrada?

670
41:24.800 --> 41:26.240
Nothing in particular.

671
41:26.600 --> 41:29.280
I just want you to examine the project carefully.

672
41:30.200 --> 41:33.200
I'm worried she might have a hidden agenda

673
41:33.200 --> 41:35.200
behind all that advertising money.

674
41:37.800 --> 41:40.840
For now, the contract says Lune

675
41:40.840 --> 41:43.480
will handle only the overall brand strategy.

676
41:43.480 --> 41:46.800
As for the finer details and other obligations,

677
41:46.800 --> 41:49.280
those are still under careful review.

678
41:50.080 --> 41:51.560
You can rest assured, Ms. Rinrada.

679
41:53.120 --> 41:54.560
Well, that's a relief.

680
41:58.000 --> 41:58.760
Oh, and...

681
41:59.680 --> 42:02.560
that new assistant of yours,

682
42:03.280 --> 42:07.120
how is she doing after her first couple of days? Is she keeping up?

683
42:09.440 --> 42:11.400
Not with everything yet.

684
42:12.320 --> 42:14.040
She's still a little flustered sometimes,

685
42:15.280 --> 42:18.320
but overall she's improving steadily.

686
42:20.200 --> 42:21.160
Auntie!

687
42:22.160 --> 42:22.960
Hello!

688
42:27.400 --> 42:28.920
Um, sorry.

689
42:29.800 --> 42:31.560
Hello, Ms. Rinrada.

690
42:36.160 --> 42:39.760
How's work in this department? Any problems?

691
42:40.640 --> 42:41.920
Hmm...

692
42:41.920 --> 42:42.880
It's fun!

693
42:42.880 --> 42:46.720
Everyone on the team is kind and always helps me.

694
42:49.040 --> 42:50.000
That's good.

695
42:50.640 --> 42:52.880
Work hard here.

696
42:53.200 --> 42:55.880
Learn as much as you can from your seniors.

697
42:57.120 --> 42:59.920
Don't waste your time wandering around, or you'll learn nothing.

698
43:01.600 --> 43:02.440
Yes.

699
43:03.040 --> 43:05.880
I'll get back to work, then.

700
43:05.880 --> 43:07.800
Work mode!

701
43:36.760 --> 43:41.360
Namhom is pretty, but her eyes look a bit empty.

702
43:44.080 --> 43:45.760
Do you have too much free time, Alice?

703
43:45.760 --> 43:46.640
You may be kind, Alice,

704
43:46.640 --> 43:48.800
but you're not very smart, are you?

705
43:48.800 --> 43:49.560
Get in.

706
43:50.280 --> 43:51.680
Or do I have to come down and pick you up?

707
43:52.120 --> 43:54.520
How can anyone drink this much tea every day?

708
43:54.960 --> 43:57.120
It stops me from killing people in meetings.

709
43:57.640 --> 43:59.800
Then you should drink plenty of it!

710
44:00.320 --> 44:02.120
You're already blushing from seeing my underwear.

711
44:02.600 --> 44:04.000
If you saw me wearing it,

712
44:04.000 --> 44:06.640
wouldn't you have a heart attack, Ms. Alice?
